{
  "fg_env": "1",
  "name": "Five Crowns",
  "description": "A Diplomacy-style game of alliances and betrayal: five nations, twenty provinces, simultaneous orders.",
  "inputs": {
    "years": {
      "type": "int",
      "default": 10,
      "min": 1,
      "max": 30,
      "description": "Years before the game ends without a winner (two seasons each)."
    },
    "win_centers": {
      "type": "int",
      "default": 10,
      "min": 2,
      "max": 16,
      "description": "Supply centers a nation needs to win outright."
    },
    "armies": {
      "type": "table",
      "description": "Starting armies (one row each). Override to set up a custom position.",
      "columns": {
        "id": "text",
        "owner": "text",
        "at": "text"
      },
      "default": [
        {
          "id": "aur_1",
          "owner": "aurelia",
          "at": "aurum"
        },
        {
          "id": "aur_2",
          "owner": "aurelia",
          "at": "silvermere"
        },
        {
          "id": "bor_1",
          "owner": "borovia",
          "at": "borsk"
        },
        {
          "id": "bor_2",
          "owner": "borovia",
          "at": "kovna"
        },
        {
          "id": "cal_1",
          "owner": "caldor",
          "at": "calder"
        },
        {
          "id": "cal_2",
          "owner": "caldor",
          "at": "emberfall"
        },
        {
          "id": "dra_1",
          "owner": "drakmar",
          "at": "drakhold"
        },
        {
          "id": "dra_2",
          "owner": "drakmar",
          "at": "ravenmoor"
        },
        {
          "id": "els_1",
          "owner": "elswyth",
          "at": "elswick"
        },
        {
          "id": "els_2",
          "owner": "elswyth",
          "at": "thornwood"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "brief": {
    "situation": "Five nations share a continent of twenty provinces. Sixteen provinces are supply centers (marked ★); each center feeds one army. Whoever holds {$inputs.win_centers} centers after an autumn wins; otherwise the game ends after year {$inputs.years}. Map — each province and the provinces it borders: {$map_text()}",
    "rules": "Each year has two seasons, Spring and Fall. Every season: (1) Negotiation — write private letters to any nation (only you and the recipient see them) and public declarations everyone sees. A letter can carry a formal pledge not to attack the recipient this season; the recipient sees the pledge. (2) Orders — all nations secretly order each of their armies at the same time: hold, move to a bordering province, or support another army's move (the supporter must border the destination). Unordered armies hold. (3) Resolution — a move's strength is 1 plus its valid supports; it takes the province if its strength beats every other move into that province and the defending army's strength (1 for an army that stays). Ties bounce and nobody moves in. You cannot dislodge your own army. Two armies trading places bounce unless one is stronger. A support is cut if the supporter is attacked by another nation from any province other than the one it supports into. (4) Retreats — a dislodged army retreats to an empty bordering province (not where the attack came from, not a province left empty by a bounce) or is destroyed; two retreats to the same province destroy both. (5) After Fall, each supply center belongs to the nation occupying it (empty centers keep their owner). Each nation then builds armies in its free, owned home centers or disbands armies until it has one army per center; whatever you leave undone is done for you.",
    "roles": {
      "nation": "You lead {$actor.name}. Your home centers: {$join($map($filter(province, $it.home == $actor.id), $it.name + ' [' + $it.id + ']'), ', ')}. Grow your nation: take supply centers, keep your armies alive, and win outright if you can. Alliances help; so can betrayal."
    }
  },
